WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.700
Speaker 1: Well, we now know that Republicans&nbsp;
have won the House in the 2022 midterms and will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:11.580
control the House of Representatives for a two&nbsp;
year period. It will be Hunter Biden 24 seven.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:17.880
It may be Joe Biden impeachment. How do we know?&nbsp;
Well, I'll show you in a moment. If you needed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:25.080
any more sense of what to expect, though, you&nbsp;
need look only over to the Senate and what 37&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:33.240
Republican senators there did in voting against&nbsp;
recognizing codifying same sex and interracial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:43.740
marriages. It's 2022. It's not 2002 or 1992&nbsp;
or 1922. But 37 Republican senators said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:51.480
let's not codify federal recognition of same sex&nbsp;
and interracial marriage. And that tells us a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:56.580
about what we can expect in the House. Now, one&nbsp;
important thing to mention, at the end of the day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:07.860
we had shifting forecasts, polls being molded like&nbsp;
putty. We didn't know well which scenario, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:13.800
most likely scenario going into the midterms was&nbsp;
Democrats hold the Senate but lose the House. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:19.980
that's exactly what happened. Now, of course, it&nbsp;
was a circuitous path to get there, but the final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:30.840
result in the 30,000 foot view is exactly what we&nbsp;
expected. Now, in terms of the Biden impeachment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:39.720
Hunter Biden investigations, these are really&nbsp;
not maybes, first and foremost. Jim Jordan will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:46.500
